With the addition of patterns/, the semantic architecture now consists of five complementary layers:

Ontology
      │
      ├── Entities      (what exists)
      ├── Relationships (how they connect)
      ├── Signals       (current state)
      ├── Patterns      (repeatable designs)
      └── Anti-Patterns (repeatable failures)
              │
              ▼
Institutional Knowledge Graph
              │
              ▼
Institutional Intelligence
              │
              ▼
Design Guidance
              │
              ▼
Governance Analytics
              │
              ▼
AI-Assisted Institutional Architecture

Patterns transform the knowledge graph from a descriptive model into a prescriptive institutional design system. They allow the IOS to recommend proven governance structures, highlight risky arrangements, and guide the construction of more resilient, interoperable, and adaptive public institutions.
